SCOPE AND CONFIGURATION
- Production equations, radial boundary, KO helper, and hot path unchanged.
- Lz=8, x=[0.5,4.5], CFL=0.05, ko_sigma=0.3, tf=8.
- epsilon=1e-8; k=pi/4 (mode 1) and pi/2 (mode 2).
- Medium: Nx=32, Nz=64, dx=dz=1/8, dt=0.00625.
- Fine: Nx=48, Nz=96, dx=dz=1/12, dt=1/240.
- Diagnostic cadence gives sample spacing 0.025 at both resolutions.
- Exactly ten evolutions: one control and four signed cases per resolution.
- No E1/E2, boundary, D6--D11, adaptive-scan, or comparison rerun.

SIGNED ANALYSIS
- odd=(plus-minus)/(2 epsilon).
- even=(plus+minus-2 control)/(2 epsilon).
- q=log(hww/chi)/2 uses both Fourier quadratures and hypot amplitudes.
- Additional phase-neutral fields: hww/chi, K, Aww, GammaX.
- Linearized H, Mx, Mz, secondary harmonic, and radial Nyquist projections
  are fixture-only.
- Rolling log-slope widths: 0.5 and 1.0, stepped by 0.25.
- Joint acceptance requires the prescribed q gates plus compatible slopes in
  all four additional fields.

